[{:db/id 17592186087658 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f69cf1ca-47a0-5c1a-89a4-ba27600434f1" "question-9985268c-7921-5895-ae59-048de6962883"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186087660 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-727fd4af-87ee-5f68-9fac-4f3bb9ee42b6" "question-ce9524f3-b3f6-5df0-a247-5d8e5bf9f0d4"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186087659 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-85a89c6d-abe9-53d6-8315-1fd338cd6cd0" "question-3df7ca0c-a7bc-5b5f-9b3f-4b5360131dc4"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-f69cf1ca-47a0-5c1a-89a4-ba27600434f1" :question/id #uuid "f69cf1ca-47a0-5c1a-89a4-ba27600434f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-7555" :question/problem "![](images/53/533a1d7aaa5cc94ed737e665189d3722582e83c3b556bce13ec0d4d0c547ffc8.png)\n\nFind the $x$-intercepts of the circle $(x-1)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}=9,$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "We must have $y=0$ at the $x$-intercepts. \n\nSo, we need to substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the circle and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-1)^{2}+(y+2)^{2} & =9 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+(0+2)^{2} & =9 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+4 & =9 \\\\ (x-1)^{2} & =5 \\\\ x-1 & =\\pm \\sqrt{5} \\\\ x & =1\\pm \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-intercepts occur at the points $(1-\\sqrt{5},0)$ and $(1+\\sqrt{5},0).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5102418c-9d09-5888-9bdb-218f5c22053d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5102418c-9d09-5888-9bdb-218f5c22053d" :answer-field/id #uuid "5102418c-9d09-5888-9bdb-218f5c22053d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8dbff389-361b-5a47-a041-221be4cfa96e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f0d3a380-0b18-5443-a78b-da9ddd47a0d7" "answer-b0f2dc27-b293-5c07-bfaf-9355e5d257f7" "answer-8dbff389-361b-5a47-a041-221be4cfa96e" "answer-6027597a-7b05-59d1-bbd7-05bf97b739c4" "answer-8b6e9076-4fad-5afe-b63f-c3d17654fc9e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f0d3a380-0b18-5443-a78b-da9ddd47a0d7" :answer/id #uuid "f0d3a380-0b18-5443-a78b-da9ddd47a0d7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-1.5,0)$ and $(3.5,0)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b0f2dc27-b293-5c07-bfaf-9355e5d257f7" :answer/id #uuid "b0f2dc27-b293-5c07-bfaf-9355e5d257f7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-2,0)$ and $(4,0)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8dbff389-361b-5a47-a041-221be4cfa96e" :answer/id #uuid "8dbff389-361b-5a47-a041-221be4cfa96e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(1-\\sqrt{5},0)$ and $(1+\\sqrt{5},0)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6027597a-7b05-59d1-bbd7-05bf97b739c4" :answer/id #uuid "6027597a-7b05-59d1-bbd7-05bf97b739c4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(2-\\sqrt{2},0)$ and $(2+\\sqrt{2},0)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8b6e9076-4fad-5afe-b63f-c3d17654fc9e" :answer/id #uuid "8b6e9076-4fad-5afe-b63f-c3d17654fc9e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(2-\\sqrt{7},0)$ and $(2+\\sqrt{7},0)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-9985268c-7921-5895-ae59-048de6962883" :question/id #uuid "9985268c-7921-5895-ae59-048de6962883" :question/math-academy-id "q-7536" :question/problem "![](images/29/299ca5fbab1351ab47dc2be6adac47b3ba3daf747e54c9b41042076cd2fee669.png)\n\nFind the $x$-intercepts of the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=5,$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "We must have $y=0$ at the $x$-intercepts. \n\nSo, we need to substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the circle and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =5 \\\\ {x}^{2}+{0}^{2} & =5 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =5 \\\\ x & =\\pm \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-intercepts occur at the points $(-\\sqrt{5},0)$ and $(\\sqrt{5},0).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8b32cc3b-6e06-50f6-9243-7fd14609227d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8b32cc3b-6e06-50f6-9243-7fd14609227d" :answer-field/id #uuid "8b32cc3b-6e06-50f6-9243-7fd14609227d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f33e6e4d-5bf4-5388-8194-4ab24fe8d402" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2320e7f1-6a2e-5cac-82f0-58db10b4f2cf" "answer-d1d5c52d-52b8-5166-bd94-8dfa858f34ac" "answer-3823a57d-2e1d-5238-8ca2-dc51024a5920" "answer-f17e7c42-6a58-58ca-8c98-85e3ba3734c9" "answer-f33e6e4d-5bf4-5388-8194-4ab24fe8d402"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2320e7f1-6a2e-5cac-82f0-58db10b4f2cf" :answer/id #uuid "2320e7f1-6a2e-5cac-82f0-58db10b4f2cf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-2,0)$ and $(2,0)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d1d5c52d-52b8-5166-bd94-8dfa858f34ac" :answer/id #uuid "d1d5c52d-52b8-5166-bd94-8dfa858f34ac" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-25,0)$ and $(25,0)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3823a57d-2e1d-5238-8ca2-dc51024a5920" :answer/id #uuid "3823a57d-2e1d-5238-8ca2-dc51024a5920" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-3,0)$ and $(3,0)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f17e7c42-6a58-58ca-8c98-85e3ba3734c9" :answer/id #uuid "f17e7c42-6a58-58ca-8c98-85e3ba3734c9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-5,0)$ and $(5,0)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f33e6e4d-5bf4-5388-8194-4ab24fe8d402" :answer/id #uuid "f33e6e4d-5bf4-5388-8194-4ab24fe8d402" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-\\sqrt{5},0)$ and $(\\sqrt{5},0)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-727fd4af-87ee-5f68-9fac-4f3bb9ee42b6" :question/id #uuid "727fd4af-87ee-5f68-9fac-4f3bb9ee42b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-54224" :question/problem "![](images/79/793009824d6d5a75f934fa3cfb60dd7e1b05b2918c6fef605777221bae3898af.png)\n\nFind the $y$-intercepts of the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+4x-6y=-5,$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "We must have $x=0$ at the $y$-intercepts. \n\nSo, we need to substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the circle and solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+4x-6y & =-5 \\\\ (0)^{2}+{y}^{2}+4(0)-6y & =-5 \\\\ {y}^{2}-6y & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this equation by completing the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-6y+9 & =-5+9 \\\\ (y-3)^{2} & =4 \\\\ y-3 & =\\pm 2 \\\\ y & =3\\pm 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-intercepts occur at the points $(0,1)$ and $(0,5).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-28942b24-6b63-5bae-98c0-24be81b19e89"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-28942b24-6b63-5bae-98c0-24be81b19e89" :answer-field/id #uuid "28942b24-6b63-5bae-98c0-24be81b19e89" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-dcaee0b5-3c30-5bb2-af72-bec250543bf1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-40b43e26-3bfb-5ad1-97a4-8c14ea7ab819" "answer-dcaee0b5-3c30-5bb2-af72-bec250543bf1" "answer-ad522c1d-8789-574e-8181-f8a71fe2ee0c" "answer-88ca8278-56f5-5e3c-bfdf-6eec82b35bb3" "answer-923eb41e-5bfd-569b-a4cd-7065f6f0f080"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-40b43e26-3bfb-5ad1-97a4-8c14ea7ab819" :answer/id #uuid "40b43e26-3bfb-5ad1-97a4-8c14ea7ab819" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,1)$ and $(0,4)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dcaee0b5-3c30-5bb2-af72-bec250543bf1" :answer/id #uuid "dcaee0b5-3c30-5bb2-af72-bec250543bf1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,1)$ and $(0,5)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ad522c1d-8789-574e-8181-f8a71fe2ee0c" :answer/id #uuid "ad522c1d-8789-574e-8181-f8a71fe2ee0c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,2)$ and $(0,6)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-88ca8278-56f5-5e3c-bfdf-6eec82b35bb3" :answer/id #uuid "88ca8278-56f5-5e3c-bfdf-6